  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY NIGHT THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 1206 PM MST Thu Nov 12 2026\n\nMonday...The flow aloft backs to southwest, inducing surface lee \ntroughing across our forecast area, and producing a continued \nwarming trend as 700 mb temperatures rise to near 6 Celsius. \nContinued dry with limited low and mid level moisture.\n\nTuesday...Looks like a breezy to windy day as the flow aloft \nstrengthens in advance of an approaching shortwave trough aloft from \nUtah and Arizona. Low and mid level moisture still looks too scant \nfor any precipitation to reach the ground.\n\nWednesday...A progressive negatively tilted shortwave trough aloft \nwill move across our counties, spreading chances for showers from \nwest to east, with somewhat drier conditions by late afternoon in \nthe wake of the shortwave trough aloft.\n\nThursday...Fast southwest flow aloft develops again ahead of the \nclosed low aloft across Idaho and Nevada. Looks like enough synoptic \nand mesoscale lift and adequate moisture to produce showers \nspreading from west to east, until the late afternoon when \nsubsidence behind the shortwave trough aloft will make it drier. 700 \nmb temperatures suggest temperatures will be somewhat similar when \ncompared to Wednesday.",
